Every has almost 30 people. Our employee agent handles stable, repeatable work, while humans frame problems, judge the output, catch errors, and turn results into decisions.



@danshipper, cofounder and CEO of Every, says each agent still needs a human for the work to, well, work. The more independently an agent operates, the worse it performs.



